
--- testing ordinal of simple choice type: ---

PASS ordinal: got 0
PASS ordinal: got 1
PASS ordinal: got 2
PASS ordinal: got 4
PASS ordinal and as_string in call to f: got ordinal is 4 for böa
PASS ordinal and as_string in call to f: got ordinal is 0 for true
PASS ordinal and as_string in call to f: got ordinal is 1 for 42
PASS ordinal and as_string in call to f: got ordinal is 2 for 98
PASS ordinal and as_string in call to f: got ordinal is 4 for hi

--- testing ordinals of some common choice types: ---

PASS true .ordinal      : got 1
PASS true .as_string: got true
PASS false.ordinal      : got 0
PASS false.as_string: got false
PASS (option String "bla").ordinal      : got 0
PASS (option String "bla").as_string: got bla
PASS (option String nil    ).ordinal      : got 1
PASS (option String nil    ).as_string: got --nil--
PASS (option i64 42 ).ordinal      : got 0
PASS (option i64 42 ).as_string: got 42
PASS (option i64 nil).ordinal      : got 1
PASS (option i64 nil).as_string: got --nil--

--- testing ordinals choice with several `void` entries: ---

PASS id (choice void void void i32 void void unit nil void void) 42   .ordinal: got 3
PASS id (choice void void void i32 void void unit nil void void) 42   .as_string: got 42
PASS id (choice void void void i32 void void unit nil void void) unit .ordinal: got 6
PASS id (choice void void void i32 void void unit nil void void) unit .as_string: got unit
PASS id (choice void void void i32 void void unit nil void void) nil  .ordinal: got 7
PASS id (choice void void void i32 void void unit nil void void) nil  .as_string: got --nil--
PASS id (choice unit void void) unit .ordinal: got 0
PASS id (choice void unit void) unit .ordinal: got 1
PASS id (choice void void unit) unit .ordinal: got 2

--- testing `option nil`, which is effectively `choice nil nil`, but it can have ordinals 0 and 1: ---

PASS id (Sequence nil) [nil] .first.ordinal:: got 0
PASS id (Sequence nil) []    .first.ordinal:: got 1

--- choice of unit types and ref types only are encoded using no tag field but special ref values by the C backend: ---

PASS id (choice unit String nil (Sequence i64) concur) unit    .ordinal: got 0
PASS id (choice unit String nil (Sequence i64) concur) 'str'   .ordinal: got 1
PASS id (choice unit String nil (Sequence i64) concur) nil     .ordinal: got 2
PASS id (choice unit String nil (Sequence i64) concur) [1,2,4] .ordinal: got 3
PASS id (choice unit String nil (Sequence i64) concur) concur  .ordinal: got 4

--- choice of only unit types are treated like an int type by the JVM backend: ---

PASS id (choice unit nil concur) unit   .ordinal: got 0
PASS id (choice unit nil concur) nil    .ordinal: got 1
PASS id (choice unit nil concur) concur .ordinal: got 2

--- testing with void alternatives ---

PASS impossible option: got nil
PASS option nil !ok: got nil --nil-- ordinal:1
PASS option nil ok!: got nil --nil-- ordinal:0
PASS option nil !ok via generic call: got matches B: --nil-- type option nil 1
PASS option nil ok! via generic call: got matches A: --nil-- type option nil 0

--- mix of void, several ref and several unit types ---

PASS blub: got 1: StringYeahYeah!
PASS blub: got 2: nil
PASS blub: got 3: Sequence [1, 2, 3, 4]
PASS blub: got 4: unit
PASS blob: got 1: StringYeahYeah!
PASS blob: got 2: nil
PASS blob: got 3: option Sequence [1, 2, 3, 4]
PASS blob: got 4: unit

